.TH ABS 3
.SH NAME
abs, labs \- integer absolute value
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
int
abs(i)
int i;

long
labs(l)
long l;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B abs
returns the absolute value of the int
.IR i ,
and
.B labs
of the long
.IR l .
.BR fabs (3)
does it for a double.
.SH SEE ALSO
floor(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B abs
function first appeared in Version 6 AT&T UNIX.
.B labs
is not in the C library of Version 7.
.SH BUGS
The most negative int, \-32768, and the most negative long,
\-2147483648, have no positive counterparts, and come back unchanged.
